course: dictionary
lesson: 8237
title: One word, more than one meaning: reward
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Leo tried a third way: homework first, then Minecraft as a reward.» Here a reward is a treat you get after doing a job first. Ask: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
explain: Reward can also be a verb, an action word. «Turning away and rewarding four paws on the floor works better.» To reward means to give someone a reward. The dog gets something good for sitting with four paws on the floor, so the word that follows tells you what is being given.
explain: Look for clues such as money or a prize. If someone offers a reward for a lost cat, the clue is the offer, and the reward is money or a prize for whoever finds it. «He finished faster, because the reward was waiting» means a prize was waiting at the end of the game.
fact: Reward means something good you get for doing something well, working hard or being helpful.
fact: A reward can also be money offered for finding something lost or helping catch a criminal.
fact: To reward someone means to give them a reward. «Rewarding» is the verb form, and «rewards» can be a noun or a verb.
fact: «Modern trainers use rewards because they work better and are kind.»
fact: Be careful online: a «reward» for clicking a link can be a trick. If a reward sounds too good to be true, ask a grown-up before you click.
exercise: «Leo tried a third way: homework first, then Minecraft as a reward.» What is the reward here? | A bad mark for forgetting homework | Money he found in the street | *Playing Minecraft after his homework | A reward chart on the wall
exercise: «Turning away and rewarding four paws on the floor works better.» What does rewarding mean here? | Sending the dog outside on its own | *Giving the dog a treat or attention for good behaviour | Taking the dog to the vet | Shouting at the dog to make it stop
exercise: A family offers a reward for their lost cat. What does reward mean here? | *Money or a prize given to whoever finds the cat | A bowl of food for the cat | A telling-off for losing the cat | A holiday for the family
test: «Rewards for playing every day are made to keep you coming back, even when you do not feel like it.» What does this suggest a reward does? | Costs you money every time you play | Stops you from playing ever again | Makes you fall asleep | *Makes you want to keep coming back
test: In «rewarding four paws on the floor», what kind of word is rewarding? | A question word | An adjective, a describing word | *A verb, an action word | A noun, a naming word
exam: Which option uses reward as a verb? | Golden time at the end of the day | *«Turning away and rewarding four paws on the floor works better.» | A reward chart on the wall | «Leo tried a third way: homework first, then Minecraft as a reward.»
